Carafe: a window's surface is placed where its pixels belong: in the part of its visible rectangle that the
window covers. win32u makes the visible rectangle of a fullscreen window in a scaled display mode cover the
whole screen, whatever its aspect, while the surface still holds the window alone, so a 4:3 window was drawn
from the screen's left edge instead of between the side bars.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/dlls/win32u/winnx_drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/winnx_drv.c
@@ -1091,6 +1091,14 @@
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+static RECT wine_nx_shown_rect( const struct window_rects *rects )
+{
+    RECT shown;
+
+    if (!intersect_rect( &shown, &rects->visible, &rects->window )) shown = rects->visible;
+    return shown;
+}
